      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67019,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> lymphangiomatosis; lymphatic dysplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67020,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67021,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphangiomatosis within the thorax frequently involves the mediastinum, with or without involvement of the heart. It may be limited to the lung and pleura.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67022,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "<p>Diffuse pulmonary lymphangiomatosis usually presents in children. It can result in mass effect from infiltrative disease, restrictive and obstructive pulmonary physiology, chylous effusions, and respiratory failure. In paediatric patients the disease has an aggressive course, with progressive respiratory failure and death. Adult patients may present with mild wheezing, non-productive cough, recurrent chylous pleural effusions, or respiratory failure {23457676; 23176925}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>On imaging, chest radiographs may show increased interstitial marking and pleural effusions. CT shows mediastinal soft tissue infiltration, pleural thickening (with effusions), thickening of peribronchovascular bundles, and interlobular septa {23457676}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-07T17:38:29"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67023,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Diffuse pulmonary lymphangiomatosis is typically diagnosed shortly after birth or during childhood, but also rarely during adulthood {22982897; 31651839}. It affects both sexes equally.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67024,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67025,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67026,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Obvious cysts or mass lesions may not be present. Diffuse pulmonary lymphangiomatosis shows lymphatic distribution as evidenced by prominence of visceral pleural, interlobular septa, and bronchovascular bundles {8276379}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67027,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Increased numbers of anastomosing, variably sized, endothelial-lined spaces containing acellular eosinophilic material are distributed along the lymphatic routes and lined by a layer of flattened lymphatic endothelial cells. Collagen layers or spindle cells resembling smooth muscle cells are present between channels. The adjacent lung tissue shows various quantities of haemosiderin-laden macrophages {8276379; 22982897}.</p>\r\n<p>The lining cells are positive for D2-40, CD31, and ERG, and the stromal spindle cells express vimentin, desmin, actin, and PR but not ER, keratin, or HMB45 {8276379; 22982897}.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnoses include lymphangioleiomyomatosis, lymphangiectasis, haemangiomatosis, and Kaposi sarcoma. Lymphangioleiomyomatosis contains HMB45-positive spindle cells. Lymphangiectasis does not show an increased number of anastomosing lymphatic vessels. Kaposi sarcoma does not show the complex anastomosing lymphatic canals. In haemangiomatosis, vascular spaces are blood-filled.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67028,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "<p>In the setting of chylous effusions where there is milky pleural fluid, cytology can show lymphocytes within lymphatic fluid, although this is not specific for diagnosis {31651839}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-07T17:38:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67029,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67030,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Increased numbers of cytologically bland anastomosing lymphatic channels distributed along the lymphatic routes</li>\r\n<li>Positive staining for lymphatic markers (e.g. D2-40)</li>\r\n<li>No cytological features of malignancy</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T10:28:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67031,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67032,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 98,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognosis is poor; there is no established curative treatment. However, recent case studies have reported improved outcome with bevacizumab and sildenafil {30510764; 31015245}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T11:19:59"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]